==Esperanto==
{{wp|lang=eo}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|eo|en|OK}} {{see desc}}. Not to be confused with {{m|eo|ok|t=eight}} or {{m|eo|oke|t=eighthly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|eo|LL-Q143 (epo)-Lepticed7-okej.wav|Audio}}
{{eo-IPA}}

===Interjection===
{{eo-intj}}

# {{lb|eo|neologism|informal}} [[okay]], [[OK]]
#: {{syn|eo|bone|en ordo|konsentite}}

===Usage notes===

Because the spelling ''okej'' indicates that the stress is placed on the penultimate (i.e. first) syllable, it is sometimes spelled ''[[o kej]]'' or ''[[ho kej]]'' to render the common pronunciation with the stress on the final syllable (as in English).

